   "confidence": "datasheet",
   "note": "The product page prints \"444 mm x 300 mm x 44 mm (17.48 in x 11.81 in x 1.73 in)\" labelled L x W x H, one row for both sizes. Read with the photographs and the 1U height, 444 is the width of the body between the ear folds, 300 the depth and 44 the height. The label's order does not say so, and no drawing confirms it."
  },
  "colour": {
   "confidence": "photo-measured",
   "note": "The front and rear are black, the jacks have bright metal shields, the USB tongues are blue, the rack ears are black and the thumbscrews have a blue ring."
  },
  "ears": {
   "confidence": "photo-measured",
   "note": "The front photograph shows a rack ear on each side, flush with the face and holding two slotted holes. The page says nothing of ears or a rail kit. No position other than the one photographed is stated, and no distance behind the face is measured."
  },
  "front-layout": {
   "confidence": "photo-measured",
   "note": "From the front photograph: two Ethernet jacks stacked at 24.1, two SFP+ cages stacked at 43.0, the console jack and two USB Type A ports in one housing centred at 69.4, and sixteen serial jacks in two rows, the odd numbers below, from 83.85 on a 14.2 pitch. The pitch was read off the numerals twice, in this photograph and in the 48-port front, and sits 1.6 per cent above the registry's 13.97. The row of round vents along the top runs from 82 to 429 on a 4.15 pitch. The power and status lamps are at 19.0, 18.5 and 24.3 down; the round button below them is at 10.5, 34.3 down."
  },
  "gate-1": {
   "confidence": "photo-measured",
   "note": "The front photograph spans 678 px for the 444 mm body between the ears (1.53 px/mm) and the rear 731 px for the 444 mm body (1.65 px/mm). The photographs include the top edge of the box, so across is read at the scale above and down is a fraction of the face's own height (44 mm) read off its top and bottom edges. Every position is good to about 2 mm."
  },
  "lamps": {
   "confidence": "datasheet",
   "note": "The page lists \"Front: device power, status; (2) Ethernet (link/active) console (Tx/Rx); 16/48 (Tx/Rx); Back: (2) PSU, status, WWAN signal/service\". The rear photograph prints WWAN Signal, WWAN Service, PSU1, PSU2 and Status. Nothing states a colour or a state, so the system lamps carry on and off only."
  },
  "ports": {
   "confidence": "datasheet",
   "note": "The product page lists \"(16) RS-232 serial RJ-45 (support standard or reversed mode)\", \"(1) RS-232 serial RJ-45 console port\", \"(2) 10/100/1000 Ethernet\", \"(2) 10 Gb capable SFP+ sockets\", \"(2) USB 3.1 Gen 1 (Type A)\" and an SD socket. The standard or reversed setting is a pinout setting and is not drawn."
  },
  "power": {
   "confidence": "datasheet",
   "note": "\"Redundant 100-240 V ~ 50-60 Hz 2.4 A max for each power supply\" and \"POWER CONSUMPTION 30.5 W\" for this size. The page does not say whether the figure is typical or maximum, so it is filed as the maximum. The mandatory kit supplies the two replaceable supplies."
  },
  "rear-layout": {
   "confidence": "photo-measured",
   "note": "From the rear photograph: the power supply bays are 94 wide at each end, the CORE plate 96 to 301, the system fan grille 40 across centred at 322.5, the SD slot and reset pinhole on a cover plate at 233.6, and five lamps at 295.5 from 13.3 down on a 5.2 pitch. The two WWAN openings are centred at 116.3 and 208.0, 31.4 down, about 7 mm across."
  },
